// 1. for each layer $\ell$, KV cache $X \in \mathbb{R}^{B\times H\times T\times d}$ do
// 2.   $r \leftarrow$ residual_length; if $\ell \in \{0, L-1\}$: $r \leftarrow \lfloor 1.5\,r\rfloor$
// 3.   keep last $r$ tokens FP16; let $X_q$ be the first $T-r$ tokens
// 4.   if KEY:  reshape per-channel groups $g$ along token axis; $\hat g = \mathrm{minmax\_quant}(g, b)$
// 5.   if VALUE:  flatten across heads; for each token-group $g$ of size $G$:
// 6.     $H_G \leftarrow$ normalized Walsh-Hadamard $G\times G$
// 7.     $\tilde g \leftarrow g H_G$;  $\hat{\tilde g} \leftarrow \mathrm{minmax\_quant}(\tilde g, b)$;  $\hat g \leftarrow \hat{\tilde g} H_G$
// 8.   write $\hat X_q$ back; report $\overline{b} = ((T{-}r)\,b + r\,16)/T$

// 1. for each layer KV cache $X \in \mathbb{R}^{B\times H\times T\times d}$ do
// 2.   keep last $r$ tokens FP16 (workload-dep: 128 long-context, 32 NIAH)
// 3.   reshape into groups of size $G$ along the chosen axis (channel for keys, token for values)
// 4.   for each group $g$:  $r_g = \max_g - \min_g$;  weight $w_g = \log_2 r_g$
// 5.   $b_g \leftarrow b + w_g - \overline{w}_g$  // mean-zero log-range allocation
// 6.   for $k = 1\ldots 5$: clip $b_g$ to $[1, 8]$ and redistribute the clipped surplus uniformly to in-bound groups
// 7.   $q_{\max,g} \leftarrow 2^{b_g} - 1$;  scale $\leftarrow r_g/q_{\max,g}$;  asymmetric quantize each group
// 8.   report $\overline{b}$ assuming budget bits per quantized token (sum of $b_g$ unaccounted)

// 1. during prefill: collect $\overline{q}_g, \overline{q}_{prefix}, \overline{q}_{suffix}, q_{peak}$ per layer
// 2.   layer profile $p_\ell \leftarrow (0.6\overline{q}_g + 0.8\overline{q}_{suffix} + 0.3 q_{peak}) / (0.7\overline{q}_g + 0.3\overline{q}_{prefix})$
// 3. for each layer / KV kind:
// 4.   bits $\leftarrow$ piecewise on $(p_\ell, \ell/L)$ in $\{2,3,4\}$
// 5.   recent_keep $\leftarrow$ 32 (+32 long-ctx, +32 value, +32 if $p>1.2$, +32 if $p>1.45$)
// 6.   anchor_keep $\leftarrow$ 8 (+8 long-ctx, +8 value, +8 if $p>1.3$)
// 7.   importance$_t \leftarrow \overline{X^2}_{B,H,d} + 0.1 \max|X|_t$, weighted by linear ramp
// 8.   keep last recent_keep + top-$k$ anchor tokens FP16; quantize the rest at bits with min-max + clip $\in\{0.92, 0.95, 0.96\}$
// 9.   for keys, also try alt axis and pick the one with lower $\|q-X\|^2$

// 1. during prefill at layer $\ell$:  $A = \mathrm{softmax}(QK^\top / \sqrt{d})$
// 2.   per head $h$:  $\bar e_h = \overline{-\sum_k a_{\cdot,k} \log a_{\cdot,k}}$;  $\mathrm{imp}_h(t) = \overline{\max_k a_{t,k}}_B$
// 3.   ratio $\eta_h \leftarrow 0.05 + 0.15\,\mathrm{clip}((3 - \bar e_h)/2, 0, 1)$;  $k_h \leftarrow \lceil \eta_h T\rceil$
// 4.   $S_{\ell,h} \leftarrow \mathrm{topk}(\mathrm{imp}_h, k_h)$  // important position set
// 5. at decode for layer $\ell$, head $h$:
// 6.   bits$_h \leftarrow$ piecewise: 8 if $\bar e_h \le 1$; 6 if $\le 2$; 4 if $\le 3$; else 2  (clip to $[2, 8]$)
// 7.   keep tokens $\in S_{\ell,h}$ in FP16; quantize the rest with signed asym. min-max (per-channel for K, per-token for V)
// 8.   values capped at 4 bits; report layer-average bits accordingly
